.SS "void p4est_init (sc_log_handler_t log_handler, int log_threshold)"

.PP
Registers \fBp4est\fP with the SC Library and sets the logging behavior\&. This function is optional\&. This function must only be called before additional threads are created\&. If this function is not called or called with log_handler == NULL, the default SC log handler will be used\&. If this function is not called or called with log_threshold == SC_LP_DEFAULT, the default SC log threshold will be used\&. The default SC log settings can be changed with sc_set_log_defaults ()\&. 
.PP
\fBExamples\fP
.in +1c
\fBparticles/particles2\&.c\fP, \fBpoints/generate_points2\&.c\fP, \fBsimple/simple2\&.c\fP, \fBsimple/simple3\&.c\fP, \fBspheres/spheres2\&.c\fP, \fBsteps/p4est_step1\&.c\fP, \fBsteps/p4est_step3\&.c\fP, \fBtest_coordinates2\&.c\fP, \fBtimings/timings2\&.c\fP, and \fBuserdata/userdata2\&.c\fP\&.
.SS "int p4est_is_initialized (void)"

.PP
Return whether \fBp4est\fP has been initialized or not\&. Keep in mind that \fBp4est_init\fP is an optional function but it helps with proper parallel logging\&.
.PP
Currently there is no inverse to \fBp4est_init\fP, and no way to deinit it\&. This is ok since initialization generally does no harm\&. Just do not call libsc's finalize function while \fBp4est\fP is still in use\&.
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
True if \fBp4est\fP has been initialized with a call to \fBp4est_init\fP and false otherwise\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const char* p4est_version (void)"

.PP
Return the full version of \fBp4est\fP\&. 
.PP
